    "background_story": "Katherine was a skilled medieval knight who fought bravely in the Crusades. During a fierce battle, she found herself face to face with a ruthless enemy commander. As she charged forward on her horse, her opponent swung his massive broadsword in a deadly arc. Katherine attempted to dodge, but the sword caught her armor, sending her tumbling to the ground. A splintered wooden beam from a nearby barricade impaled her leg, pinning her down. Despite the excruciating pain, Katherine refused to yield. With a Herculean effort, she managed to free herself and continued fighting, her determination and valor inspiring her comrades to victory. Though her wound left her with a permanent limp, Katherine's legend as a fearless warrior endured, earning her the nickname 'The Unyielding'.",
